lue`)"],[1580,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[461,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1386,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1644,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[529,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[530,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[540,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1038,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with `errorMessage` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1238,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with `errorMessage` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1436,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1378,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1412,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1387,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[516,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1525,"\\`legendPosition\\` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with \\`null\\`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[627,"\\`MenuTrigger\\` exposes its open state via \\`isOpen\\`/\\`onOpenChange\\`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[1390,"\\`orientation=\"horizontal\"\\` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a